1
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:54,000
No one can stop the reign.

2
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:42,000
Kingdom of the Planet of the Apes is a science fiction,
adventure, action film directed by Wes Ball.

3
00:17:24,000 --> 00:17:30,000
Several generations following Caesar's reign, apes – now the dominant species – live
harmoniously while humans have been reduced to living in the shadows.

4
00:23:12,000 --> 00:23:18,000
As a new tyrannical ape leader builds his empire, one young ape undertakes a harrowing journey that will cause him to
question all he's known about the past and to make choices that will define a future for apes and humans alike.

5
00:29:00,000 --> 00:29:06,000
Noa, played by Owen Teague.

6
00:34:48,000 --> 00:34:54,000
Nova / Mae, played by Freya Allan.

7
00:40:36,000 --> 00:40:42,000
Proximus Caesar, played by Kevin Durand.

8
00:46:24,000 --> 00:46:30,000
Raka, played by Peter Macon.

9
00:52:12,000 --> 00:52:18,000
Trevathan, played by William H. Macy.

10
00:58:00,000 --> 00:58:06,000
Sylva, played by Eka Darville.

11
01:03:48,000 --> 01:03:54,000
Kingdom of the Planet of the Apes is a 2024 American science fiction
action film directed by Wes Ball and written by Josh Friedman.

12
01:09:36,000 --> 01:09:42,000
It is the fourth installment in the Planet of the Apes reboot film series and the tenth film
overall, serving as a standalone sequel to War for the Planet of the Apes (2017).

13
01:15:24,000 --> 01:15:30,000
The film stars Owen Teague, Freya Allan, Kevin
Durand, Peter Macon, and William H.

14
01:21:12,000 --> 01:21:18,000
It takes place many generations after the events of War and follows Noa (Teague), a young chimpanzee hunter who embarks
on a journey alongside Mae (Allan), a human woman, to determine the future for apes and humans alike.

15
01:27:00,000 --> 01:27:06,000
Development on a new Planet of the Apes film began in April 2019, following Disney's acquisition
of 20th Century Fox, with Ball attached as writer and director that December.

16
01:32:48,000 --> 01:32:54,000
Much of the screenplay was written during the COVID-19 pandemic in 2020, with
casting commencing in June 2022, following the screenplay's completion.

17
01:38:36,000 --> 01:38:42,000
Teague was cast in the lead role that August, with the film's title and
additional casting announced in the following months.

18
01:44:24,000 --> 01:44:30,000
Principal photography began in October 2022 in Sydney and wrapped in
February 2023, with a budget of $120–160 million.

19
01:50:12,000 --> 01:50:18,000
Kingdom of the Planet of the Apes premiered at the TCL Chinese Theatre in Los Angeles on May 2,
2024, and was released by 20th Century Studios in the United States on May 10.

20
01:56:00,000 --> 01:56:06,000
The film received generally positive reviews from critics
and grossed over $397 million worldwide.

21
02:01:48,000 --> 02:01:54,000
It received a nomination for Best Visual Effects at the 97th Academy Awards.

22
02:07:36,000 --> 02:07:42,000
A sequel is in development for an expected 2027 release.

23
02:13:24,000 --> 02:13:30,000
The film explores themes of empire, kingdom, gorilla,
dystopia, post-apocalyptic future.

24
02:19:12,000 --> 02:19:18,000
The tone is thought_provoking.
